@startuml
title Sequence diagram showing the service qualification check at the requested address

actor Customer
participant "EngagementManagement\nWeb UI" as WebUI #purple
participant "EngagementManagement\nBFF" as BFF #purple
participant "E2E SM Domain\nService Qualification Mgt" as E2ESQ #blue
participant "Fixed Access Domain\nService Qualification Mgt" as FASQ #blue
participant "Mobile Access Domain\nService Qualification Mgt" as MASQ #blue
participant "Copper Domain\nService Qualification Mgt" as COSQ #blue
participant "Product Configurator\nComponent" as PCC
participant "Product Catalog Management\nComponent" as PCM

Customer -> WebUI : 1 Enter Service Address or Landline Phone Number
WebUI -> BFF : 2 Enter Service Address or Landline Phone Number
activate BFF
BFF -> BFF : 3 validate input data

BFF -> E2ESQ : 4 **TMF 645 POST /QueryServiceQualification**  address
activate E2ESQ

E2ESQ -> FASQ : 5 **TMF 645 POST /QueryServiceQualification**  address
activate FASQ
FASQ --> E2ESQ : 6 return service(s) available for the specified address
deactivate FASQ

E2ESQ -> MASQ : 7 **TMF 645 POST /QueryServiceQualification**  address
activate MASQ
MASQ --> E2ESQ : 8 return service(s) available for the specified address
deactivate MASQ

E2ESQ -> COSQ : 9 **TMF 645 POST /QueryServiceQualification**  address
activate COSQ
COSQ --> E2ESQ : 10 return service(s) available for the specified address
deactivate COSQ

E2ESQ --> BFF : 11 return E2E Connectivity available for the specified address
deactivate E2ESQ

BFF -> PCC : 12 **TMF679 POST /productOfferingQualification**  by category, address, and channel
activate PCC
PCC -> PCC : 13 load offers

PCC -> PCM : 14 **TMF620 GET /productOffering**  by offer IDs
activate PCM
PCM --> PCC : 15
deactivate PCM

PCC -> PCC : 16 filter by category

PCC --> BFF : 17 eligible product offers
deactivate PCC

BFF --> WebUI : 18 eligible product offers
deactivate BFF
WebUI --> Customer : 19 present product offers

@enduml
